01:33:15.640 --> 01:33:17.688
the being on hold took
longer than the phone call.

01:33:17.688 --> 01:33:19.786
It was like, it's so easy.

01:33:19.786 --> 01:33:21.582
Like it's, it's so frustrating.

01:33:21.582 --> 01:33:23.914
- Whereas here it's
like, oh you're moving?

01:33:23.914 --> 01:33:26.130
- Oh you're moving? That's
a whole month process.

01:33:26.130 --> 01:33:28.007
That's not because you got to
unpack and move stuff around,

01:33:28.007 --> 01:33:29.010
that's because you got to go to the,

01:33:29.010 --> 01:33:31.492
- You gotta call up and go to
fucking in store everywhere.

01:33:31.492 --> 01:33:32.692
It's ridiculous.

01:33:32.692 --> 01:33:34.600
- So absurd. So again, we complain a lot

01:33:34.600 --> 01:33:36.167
about these aspects of Japan,

01:33:36.167 --> 01:33:37.000
but you know,

01:33:37.000 --> 01:33:39.365
we are very grateful to Japan
for allowing us to be here.

01:33:39.365 --> 01:33:40.876
- I mean, there's a reason
why you don't just leave.

01:33:40.876 --> 01:33:41.844
- Yeah we love it. You know,

01:33:41.844 --> 01:33:43.471
- We're probably going to stay here for.

01:33:43.471 --> 01:33:44.781
- I'm going to be living
in Japan for a long time.

01:33:44.781 --> 01:33:47.950
I just, you know, I think
that when you live in a place,

01:33:47.950 --> 01:33:50.437
you have the right to
complain about certain things.

01:33:50.437 --> 01:33:51.270
- Absolutely.

01:33:51.270 --> 01:33:52.852
- I complain about everywhere equally.

01:33:52.852 --> 01:33:55.379
You everywhere socks, everywhere sucks.

01:33:55.379 --> 01:33:56.846
- Exactly. There's no utopian country.

01:33:56.846 --> 01:33:58.046
- Yeah, exactly.

01:33:58.046 --> 01:33:59.051
And so, you know,

01:33:59.051 --> 01:34:01.294
I don't want people to get the idea

01:34:01.294 --> 01:34:02.825
that we're not fucking grateful.

01:34:02.825 --> 01:34:03.982
Or we're not like happy.

01:34:03.982 --> 01:34:05.454
- Because sometimes we get
comments like that sometimes.

01:34:05.454 --> 01:34:06.598
- We do get comments like that sometimes.

01:34:06.598 --> 01:34:08.086
And we are very happy here in Japan.

01:34:08.086 --> 01:34:09.661
- We're just being real
with you guys that's all.

01:34:09.661 --> 01:34:10.724
- We just, we just like to complain

01:34:10.724 --> 01:34:11.591
about the little things.

01:34:11.591 --> 01:34:13.839
You guys like it when
we're annoyed about shit.

01:34:13.839 --> 01:34:15.964
That's why we're annoyed about shit.

01:34:15.964 --> 01:34:17.254
- If you guys are going
to move to Japan. I,

01:34:17.254 --> 01:34:18.171
I want to be honest with you

01:34:18.171 --> 01:34:19.461
and tell you what's going to be fun

01:34:19.461 --> 01:34:20.431
and what's gonna suck.

01:34:20.431 --> 01:34:21.264
- There's going to be,

01:34:21.264 --> 01:34:22.389
there's going to be lots of

01:34:22.389 --> 01:34:23.320
fucking great things about it,

01:34:23.320 --> 01:34:25.304
but just be prepared for
those little conveniences.

01:34:25.304 --> 01:34:27.637
- Whenever you have to do
anything to do with like

01:34:27.637 --> 01:34:29.334
Japanese bureaucracy or just setting,

01:34:29.334 --> 01:34:32.584
setting up your living situation. I, I,

01:34:33.782 --> 01:34:36.270
- You will be writing your name, address,

01:34:36.270 --> 01:34:38.960
and phone number more times
than you'll ever think.

01:34:38.960 --> 01:34:42.544
- You will lose at least a
week just trying to figure out.

01:34:42.544 --> 01:34:43.798
- Yeah I think that's
the thing that annoys me.

01:34:43.798 --> 01:34:45.982
In the UK when I had to deal
with this stuff, it was,

01:34:45.982 --> 01:34:48.567
it was maybe an hour
out of my day at most.

01:34:48.567 --> 01:34:49.894
And I'd get on with my day.

01:34:49.894 --> 01:34:52.225
If it happens here, it
derails your whole week,

01:34:52.225 --> 01:34:53.183
like it takes a completely,

01:34:53.183 --> 01:34:54.693
you have to reschedule everything,

01:34:54.693 --> 01:34:55.946
cancel everything you're doing

01:34:55.946 --> 01:34:57.480
because you've got a call from the bank

01:34:57.480 --> 01:34:58.643
and they said that your card is canceled

01:34:58.643 --> 01:35:01.502
and they didn't tell you
until now it's canceled.

01:35:01.502 --> 01:35:02.512
- I just remembered, like,

01:35:02.512 --> 01:35:04.043
I don't know if you guys have in the UK,

01:35:04.043 --> 01:35:06.568
but like in Japanese
and Australian airports,

01:35:06.568 --> 01:35:08.865
there's like sometimes
that service where like,

01:35:08.865 --> 01:35:10.863
you know how on your suitcase,

01:35:10.863 --> 01:35:13.349
you can put like a belt around
it so it doesn't burst open.

01:35:13.349 --> 01:35:16.204
Some people forget that or,
you know, don't buy that.

01:35:16.204 --> 01:35:17.135
- I've never had to use that.

01:35:17.135 --> 01:35:17.968
- No.

01:35:17.968 --> 01:35:18.801
- So instead you can, like,

01:35:18.801 --> 01:35:20.520
you can use a service that
you can like wrap up your bag

01:35:20.520 --> 01:35:21.353
in like plastic.

01:35:21.353 --> 01:35:22.436
- [Connor] I see that in the UK. Yeah.

01:35:22.436 --> 01:35:24.275
- In Australia it's like
10 seconds you just like,

01:35:24.275 --> 01:35:25.775
wrap this up. Here's the money.

01:35:25.775 --> 01:35:27.453
They do it. All right. See you later.

01:35:27.453 --> 01:35:29.621
I did it in Haneda once in Japan.

01:35:29.621 --> 01:35:30.454
And they were like,

01:35:30.454 --> 01:35:31.618
"Okay, can you fill out this form?

01:35:31.618 --> 01:35:34.287
"Write your name, address
and phone number."

01:35:34.287 --> 01:35:36.545
I'm like, I'm never
going to see you again.

01:35:36.545 --> 01:35:38.427
Just wrap up my goddamn bag.

01:35:38.427 --> 01:35:40.800
- Get the fucking cling
film out, wrap it around

01:35:40.800 --> 01:35:42.230
and I'll give you 20 bucks.

01:35:42.230 --> 01:35:44.276
- I like deadass, I looked
at this woman. I was like,

01:35:44.276 --> 01:35:45.820
what do you need this for?

01:35:45.820 --> 01:35:46.903
Like, why do you need to know my name,

01:35:46.903 --> 01:35:47.859
phone number and address?

01:35:47.859 --> 01:35:48.692
And they're like,

01:35:48.692 --> 01:35:49.696
"Oh you know, like just in case."

01:35:49.696 --> 01:35:52.828
I'm like, because you're
wrapping my bag in plastic.

01:35:52.828 --> 01:35:53.876
- I'm a customer.

01:35:53.876 --> 01:35:55.916
I will do it myself.
Give me the cling film.

01:35:55.916 --> 01:35:57.042
- Yeah give me the cling wrap.

01:35:57.042 --> 01:35:59.525
I'll fucking do it myself.

01:35:59.525 --> 01:36:01.316
- I will pay you to not fill in that form.

01:36:01.316 --> 01:36:02.193
- It was ridiculous.

01:36:02.193 --> 01:36:03.331
- It's frustrating, man.

01:36:03.331 --> 01:36:04.510
- And I just wasted, like, you know,

01:36:04.510 --> 01:36:07.302
two minutes of my life filling
out this form, that for one,

01:36:07.302 --> 01:36:08.724
I don't even know what
they're going to use it for,

01:36:08.724 --> 01:36:10.587
but second of all, completely unnecessary.

01:36:10.587 --> 01:36:11.420
- It's just frustrating

01:36:11.420 --> 01:36:13.644
giving out your whole
fucking information to,

01:36:13.644 --> 01:36:16.688
to shit that you feel like it
just totally doesn't need it.

01:36:16.688 --> 01:36:18.502
Like, I just don't want to deal with that.

01:36:18.502 --> 01:36:19.335
I hate doing that.

01:36:19.335 --> 01:36:21.546
- But it's also like, you
know, I feel as well like,

01:36:21.546 --> 01:36:23.414
there's so many situations

01:36:23.414 --> 01:36:25.557
where you're canceling
something or, you know,

01:36:25.557 --> 01:36:26.921
you're upgrading something. Right?

01:36:26.921 --> 01:36:27.754
And you're just like,

01:36:27.754 --> 01:36:29.074
"All right, can you write your
phone number and address?"

01:36:29.074 --> 01:36:29.956
And I'm like,

01:36:29.956 --> 01:36:32.387
I'm pretty sure all my
information is on system.

01:36:32.387 --> 01:36:34.591
Just look it up. I'll
give you my fucking name.

01:36:34.591 --> 01:36:35.424
Just look it up.

01:36:35.424 --> 01:36:36.260
- If it changes, I'll let you know.

01:36:36.260 --> 01:36:37.095
I'll keep you updated.

01:36:37.095 --> 01:36:37.928
- Like how often do you think

01:36:37.928 --> 01:36:39.041
I'm changing my name and address?

01:36:39.041 --> 01:36:42.126
- Like one, one thing I'm
fucking dreading when we move,

01:36:42.126 --> 01:36:44.712
because we're all planning to
move from where we are now.

01:36:44.712 --> 01:36:47.327
I mean, you're already
in process of moving

01:36:47.327 --> 01:36:48.666
is just the process of

01:36:48.666 --> 01:36:52.456
changing my address in
every bill that I've had.

01:36:52.456 --> 01:36:55.953
And I'm just, I wake up
in a cold sweat at night

01:36:55.953 --> 01:36:56.867
sometimes being like,

01:36:56.867 --> 01:36:58.753
I gotta do that. I gotta do that.

01:36:58.753 --> 01:37:00.999
- I have been suffering
for the past month on that

01:37:00.999 --> 01:37:03.046
and it shouldn't be a suffering thing.

01:37:03.046 --> 01:37:03.920
- It just sucks because I feel like

01:37:03.920 --> 01:37:06.214
your life just comes to a
halt for a month because

01:37:06.214 --> 01:37:08.295
they've designed systems that make it so.

01:37:08.295 --> 01:37:10.219
- Yeah. And it's got nothing
to do with like, you know,

01:37:10.219 --> 01:37:12.804
people who don't understand the language,

01:37:12.804 --> 01:37:13.637
having a hard time, no.

01:37:13.637 --> 01:37:15.586
Even if you're fully Japanese,

01:37:15.586 --> 01:37:17.590
it's still hard as shit to do.

01:37:17.590 --> 01:37:18.800
And it shouldn't be that hard to do.

01:37:18.800 --> 01:37:22.010
- Like you get pretty good
customer service in most aspects

01:37:22.010 --> 01:37:24.175
of, of Japanese life I think.

01:37:24.175 --> 01:37:26.976
But for some reason with
personal information companies,

01:37:26.976 --> 01:37:28.986
I feel like it comes to
a halt and it doesn't,

01:37:28.986 --> 01:37:30.156
it doesn't improve at all.

01:37:30.156 --> 01:37:32.370
The customer service
isn't any better for it.

01:37:32.370 --> 01:37:33.695
I think that's why I think

01:37:33.695 --> 01:37:36.276
Japan has one of the lowest
productivities out of,

01:37:36.276 --> 01:37:37.824
of first world countries.

01:37:37.824 --> 01:37:38.913
- I'm not surprised.

01:37:38.913 --> 01:37:40.214
- Because they work the most.

01:37:40.214 --> 01:37:42.511
- We would have flying cars by now.

01:37:42.511 --> 01:37:45.186
- They work more hours
than any other country

01:37:45.186 --> 01:37:46.979
and have less to show for
it. You know what I mean?

01:37:46.979 --> 01:37:48.733
Like, you know, I think
in some European countries

01:37:48.733 --> 01:37:51.064
they're considering a
four day workweek even,

01:37:51.064 --> 01:37:53.148
and you know I was just like, fantastic.

01:37:53.148 --> 01:37:55.185
- You bring that up to
government officials in Japan

01:37:55.185 --> 01:37:56.018
they're like.

01:37:56.018 --> 01:37:57.645
"How does, how does that country run?"

01:37:57.645 --> 01:38:00.699
"How is that not a third world country?"

01:38:00.699 --> 01:38:02.203
"How's their economy not
crumbling to the ground?"

01:38:02.203 --> 01:38:04.454
- Again. It's just
like, how do you fix it?

01:38:04.454 --> 01:38:07.875
When everything in society has
been made to be long-winded,

01:38:07.875 --> 01:38:10.443
bloated and slow? Like, what do you do?

01:38:10.443 --> 01:38:11.316
Like how do you fix that?

01:38:11.316 --> 01:38:12.705
'Cause it's like a whole
cultural thing at that point.

01:38:12.705 --> 01:38:13.538
- Well this is a country where,

01:38:13.538 --> 01:38:16.819
a lot of schools are
still six days a week.

01:38:16.819 --> 01:38:19.985
It's ridiculous. Let alone
four day workweek what?

01:38:19.985 --> 01:38:20.818
- Yeah I mean,

01:38:20.818 --> 01:38:22.445
it took like a fucking
global pandemic, right?

01:38:22.445 --> 01:38:25.449
For the country to
embrace working from home

01:38:25.449 --> 01:38:27.115
and online meetings. Right?

01:38:27.115 --> 01:38:28.616
It's like.

01:38:28.616 --> 01:38:31.113
- They were throwing out
like the buzzword of like

01:38:31.113 --> 01:38:33.608
home workstation or whatever
the fuck it was like,

01:38:33.608 --> 01:38:36.280
it was a new thing that was
just invented. It's like,

01:38:36.280 --> 01:38:38.328
we've come up with this
revolutionary thing.

01:38:38.328 --> 01:38:41.498
Get this, you can work from home.

01:38:41.498 --> 01:38:43.415
And Japanese people
are like, "Impossible."

01:38:43.415 --> 01:38:44.567
That that is.

01:38:44.567 --> 01:38:45.425
- Telework.

01:38:45.425 --> 01:38:46.478
- Telework that's it.

01:38:46.478 --> 01:38:47.311
- Telework.

01:38:47.311 --> 01:38:48.380
- They call it telework.

01:38:48.380 --> 01:38:50.036
- I think also, I think they're now

01:38:50.036 --> 01:38:52.184
slowly starting to phase
out the hanko because of it.

01:38:52.184 --> 01:38:53.640
They're finally putting in like,

01:38:53.640 --> 01:38:55.764
the government they're
bringing it up. And trying.

01:38:55.764 --> 01:38:58.103
- Have we ever explained
hankos? I don't think we have.

01:38:58.103 --> 01:39:01.638
- Hanko are basically, is
like the, it's like a stamp

01:39:01.638 --> 01:39:04.358
essentially that has your
surname on it or, you know,

01:39:04.358 --> 01:39:05.319
company name or whatever.

01:39:05.319 --> 01:39:08.778
Basically it's the Japanese
equivalent of a signature.

01:39:08.778 --> 01:39:11.120
But incredibly tedious.

01:39:11.120 --> 01:39:12.538
- It's incredibly tedious because

01:39:12.538 --> 01:39:14.877
that means you have to
carry your hanko everywhere.

01:39:14.877 --> 01:39:15.710
- Yeah.

01:39:15.710 --> 01:39:18.178
- Whenever you're like, if you forget.

01:39:18.178 --> 01:39:19.809
- I've had moments where I'm like,

01:39:19.809 --> 01:39:21.725
I have everything except the hanko

01:39:21.725 --> 01:39:23.602
and they just don't accept it.

01:39:23.602 --> 01:39:26.187
And I'm just like, this is a
stamp I bought at Don Quijote.

01:39:26.187 --> 01:39:27.397
for like 200 yen.

01:39:27.397 --> 01:39:29.145
Don Quijote is like the dollar shop here.

01:39:29.145 --> 01:39:30.726
You can, you can just
get it at a dollar shop.

01:39:30.726 --> 01:39:32.820
- Imagine your name is Connor, right?

01:39:32.820 --> 01:39:34.576
And then, you know, you can, you know,

01:39:34.576 --> 01:39:35.452
you can go those gift shops

01:39:35.452 --> 01:39:36.660
and they have like the license plates,

01:39:36.660 --> 01:39:38.199
like Connor. It's like that.

01:39:38.199 --> 01:39:40.113
Like imagine you just go to the store,

01:39:40.113 --> 01:39:41.953
you find your name on the license plate

01:39:41.953 --> 01:39:43.085
and then you bring it and go look,

01:39:43.085 --> 01:39:45.548
it's my name. It's my
name, take a picture.

01:39:45.548 --> 01:39:46.923
- The thing is, is like, I,

01:39:46.923 --> 01:39:50.278
I wrote up a thing as to why
Japan still uses the hanko

01:39:50.278 --> 01:39:53.768
and not signatures and
the most accepted like,

01:39:53.768 --> 01:39:54.609
excuse, I guess,

01:39:54.609 --> 01:39:56.628
I'm just going to call
it an excuse as they,

01:39:56.628 --> 01:39:59.875
as why they don't use
signatures, they were like,

01:39:59.875 --> 01:40:02.082
"Well, anyone can copy a signature."

01:40:02.082 --> 01:40:06.082
Anyone can go to Don
Quijote and buy a $2 stamp.

01:40:07.208 --> 01:40:08.522
What are you on?

01:40:08.522 --> 01:40:09.600
- Yeah. It's so dumb.

01:40:09.600 --> 01:40:11.731
Yeah. I mean, if you have a popular name.

01:40:11.731 --> 01:40:12.564
- Yeah.

01:40:12.564 --> 01:40:15.163
- What happens if you have
a popular name, right?

01:40:15.163 --> 01:40:16.669
- What is it? What is it?

01:40:16.669 --> 01:40:18.381
What's the one that you see,
Tanaka? Is that the one?

01:40:18.381 --> 01:40:20.343
- Yeah Tanaka or like
Sato or like any of like

01:40:20.343 --> 01:40:21.635
the common ones.

01:40:21.635 --> 01:40:23.302
- Everyone probably,

01:40:24.329 --> 01:40:25.395
every Sato probably has

01:40:25.395 --> 01:40:27.598
the same fucking Don Quijote stamp.

01:40:27.598 --> 01:40:30.061
I'm like, this is bullshit.

01:40:30.061 --> 01:40:33.102
Like signature is way harder
to copy than buying a stamp.

01:40:33.102 --> 01:40:35.481
- Did you hear about the
fucking Josh battle royale

01:40:35.481 --> 01:40:36.314
that happened recently?

01:40:36.314 --> 01:40:37.147
- [Connor] Yeah yeah.

01:40:37.147 --> 01:40:37.980
- [Joey] What?

01:40:37.980 --> 01:40:38.813
- [Garnt] Did you hear about this?

01:40:38.813 --> 01:40:39.813
- [Joey] No.

01:40:41.286 --> 01:40:43.465
- So like, I think like a year ago,

01:40:43.465 --> 01:40:46.266
some guy in like some state or something,

01:40:46.266 --> 01:40:48.604
he looked up every, he was, his name was,

01:40:48.604 --> 01:40:49.858
- Josh Swain. Josh Swain.

01:40:49.858 --> 01:40:50.691
- Josh Wayne?

01:40:50.691 --> 01:40:51.524
- Josh Swain.

01:40:51.524 --> 01:40:52.357
- Josh Swain.

01:40:52.357 --> 01:40:54.241
He looked up like every Josh on Facebook

01:40:54.241 --> 01:40:56.998
in his area and added
them to a group right?

01:40:56.998 --> 01:40:58.286
And he just sends a message,

01:40:58.286 --> 01:41:00.912
"Guys. You know why we're here."

01:41:00.912 --> 01:41:02.581
- We're going to battle
for name Josh Swain.

01:41:02.581 --> 01:41:04.456
- [Garnt] There are already Joshes here.

01:41:04.456 --> 01:41:06.331
We are going to have a
battle royale and whoever,

01:41:06.331 --> 01:41:09.506
whoever emerges victorious
can keep the name Josh.

01:41:09.506 --> 01:41:12.297
- So that's how it works with hankos.

01:41:12.297 --> 01:41:13.653
- There's literally a movie.

01:41:13.653 --> 01:41:15.005
- I feel like they have to
do that with hankos right?

01:41:15.005 --> 01:41:15.838
- There's literally

01:41:15.838 --> 01:41:17.606
a fucking battle royale movie in Japan

01:41:17.606 --> 01:41:19.707
where it's that exact same concept.

01:41:19.707 --> 01:41:20.540
- Is it really?

01:41:20.540 --> 01:41:21.408
- Yeah yeah. It's called, it's called

01:41:21.408 --> 01:41:23.500
"Riaru Onigokko", "Real Tag"

01:41:23.500 --> 01:41:24.460
where basically it's,

01:41:24.460 --> 01:41:25.836
it's like a survival horror movie.

01:41:25.836 --> 01:41:27.508
It's actually a really
good movie and book,

01:41:27.508 --> 01:41:30.259
but basically in the it's
set in like the future

01:41:30.259 --> 01:41:33.014
where the king of Japan, his name is Sato,

01:41:33.014 --> 01:41:35.513
which is the most common surname in Japan.

01:41:35.513 --> 01:41:36.346
And he's like,

01:41:36.346 --> 01:41:38.384
"I want to be the only Sato."

